WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:09.570
Until today, I thought being a professional was about doing your job consistently.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.030
Ball!

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.620
But...

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.450
I guess I was wrong.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.420
Shouldering another's dream is also part of being a pro!

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.670
Safe!

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.180
It's about the trade you asked me to make.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.220
Oh, what's the news?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.670
We simply need to formalize the contract.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.730
He should be able to play in a few days.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.890
Really?

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.550
Good job.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.740
This will draw even bigger crowds.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.850
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.850
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:10.150
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:10.150
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:15.530
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:15.530
the only thing I truly have

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.830
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.830
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:26.160
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:26.160
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.420
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.420
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.800
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.800
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.890
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.890
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:48.440
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:48.440
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:52.520
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:52.520
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.820
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.820
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:04.080
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:04.080
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:09.750
namida kareru made

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:09.750
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.800
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.800
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.140
namida hareru made

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.140
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.140
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:25.140
though I may lose my way,

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.980
egakikake no ima

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.980
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.480
kizamu

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:36.230
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.770
akashi

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.230
kono te de

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.970
The Unspoken Rule

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.970
The Unspoken Rule

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.890
Now hitting, number 1: Jeff Keene!

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.120
It's out of here!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.500
Keene hits a home run in the ninth inning for a comeback win!

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.580
All right!

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.480
This is the fourth consecutive win for the Hornets.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.000
The league-leading Coyotes lost their game today, so the Hornets are only two games back!

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.800
Including today's game, we're thirteen and five in the second half of the season.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:27.060
We usually start falling apart in the summer, but we're holding up pretty well this year.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.000
Oh, yeah.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.270
We haven't won a league title in a while.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:33.400
Yeah.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.270
The last time we played in the World Series was twenty-five years ago,

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.400
and we haven't even won a division title since.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.750
We finally have a chance this year.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:43.610
Yeah.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.330
If we can keep this pace up, winning the title will be a breeze.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.580
If that happens, we'll be the center of attention!

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.930
And girls will be swarming around us.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.700
All right!

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.660
Let's win this, even if it kills us!

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.300
Yeah!

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:08.670
I want to bathe in champagne.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:12.230
I bet the champagne fight in the majors is nothing like the minors.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.980
Yeah.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:17.350
I'd like to let Greene get a taste of that too.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.130
Then let's do it!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.580
We'll run into his hospital room and pour champagne all over him!

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.160
The scary part is that we know you'd actually do it.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.230
Though I'm sure he'll be out of the hospital by then.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.790
About the replacement for Greene...

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.460
The new player joining us was decided today; the last day for player trades.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.210
Who exactly is it?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.500
A guy from the Los Angeles Panthers.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.670
His name's Mike Murdoch.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.500
Wh-What?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.730
Mad Murdoch?

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.470
Are you serious?

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:53.890
Wh-Who's this Murdoch guy?

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.440
Is there a problem?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.870
A problem?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.920
He's a huge problem.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.700
From what I've heard, he greets people he doesn't like by punching them.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:11.110
I've even heard that if you were to pile up his victims, they'd be higher than the Statue of Liberty.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:15.080
I heard that he wasn't even scratched when he got hit by a car.

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:19.840
S-Someone told me that he killed a bear with his bare hands.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:22.510
Wait... is he even human?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.420
Why <i>him</i>, of all players?

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.960
This is why we haven't taken the title in twenty-five years.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.080
Well, there are a lot of rumors going around about Murdoch,

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.770
but his baseball record isn't bad.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.190
Then there's nothing to worry about!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.810
As a pitcher, all I ask from him is some runs.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:49.110
I've been treated as a troublemaker too, so maybe we'll get along.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.080
Why Murdoch?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.460
He's a wonderful power hitter.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.540
Is there a problem?

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.370
I'm sure you know about his personality.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:04.630
Ever since he was in the minors, he's back-talked refs and coaches,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.330
started arguments with his teammates and fans,

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:12.180
picked fights on the field, and the list goes on and on.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.890
When the team is coming together so well, we shouldn't need to—

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.890
So what?

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.240
Fights?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:23.220
Very well, let him fight!

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.120
We'll get attention and the crowds will love it!

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.410
This is business, you see.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.480
I just need a bigger audience.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.690
Well, please have him play starting tomorrow.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.670
T-Tomorrow?!

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.490
Of course.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.900
I paid a lot of money for him.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.720
Put him to work as soon as possible.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.890
Hey, everyone!

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:15.840
Gather around.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.540
He's already here?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:25.500
Shoot.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.430
Well, look at that.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.100
He's not as crazy as I thought.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.850
He swings well too.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.870
He's a good trade.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.630
Well, of course.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.570
No one starts a fight on the first day after the trade.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.200
Good evening, everyone.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.080
The Hornets are carrying momentum as they start a three-game series against the Minneapolis Suns tonight.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:42.820
Shigeno will be their starting pitcher, with two wins under his belt in this half of the season.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.160
In other news,

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:51.340
Mike Murdoch was traded and is starting at first base and batting fifth today.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:55.300
What will he show us on his new team, the Hornets?

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.490
Play ball!

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.110
Here, pass!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.620
That was close!

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.290
You all right, Shigeno?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.160
Y-Yeah.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:30.850
Hey, you—

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:31.840
Hey!

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.550
That was dangerous!

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.420
It would've been an easy out if you had thrown it!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.770
Are you talking to me?

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:39.970
Y-Yeah...

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:47.140
If I throw, there's a risk that he'll drop it.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.840
If I think I can make it, I'll do it myself.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.320
You better watch out next time.

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.830
Strike out!

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:17.880
At least it looks like Shigeno's all right.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:18.770
Yeah.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.720
Man, that Murdoch...

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.850
That was such a dangerous play.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:28.430
Shigeno's not exactly the patient type.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.770
If Murdoch keeps taunting him, he's going to pop.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.420
Ball!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.660
Ball four!

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:50.260
All right!

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.640
A great chance with one out and the bases loaded!

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:55.090
Raynolds isn't doing so well today!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.840
Let's take him down!

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:00.450
Now hitting, number 33:

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:03.890
Mike Murdoch!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:17.860
Out!

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:20.280
Out!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.850
Hey, what?

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.530
Raynolds has terrible control today,

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:30.180
yet he swung into a double play on the first pitch?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:33.380
Man, what a rough first inning.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.660
This is what I was afraid of.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:41.990
Murdoch has good numbers on paper, but he ruins good chances.

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:47.730
He can't do any type of team batting like sacrifice flies.

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.600
Yeah.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.700
He hasn't stayed on any team for very long

00:11:52.700 --> 00:12:00.280
because he's been seen as a curse that keeps their standings low.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.820
Well, we can't do anything now that he's here,

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.850
but I hope he doesn't become a curse for us.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:22.670
Out!

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.690
Raynolds got another two outs easily.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:29.000
He's completely back on his feet.

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.690
And Murdoch's up next.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.810
You better show us something good this time!

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.190
This is bad.

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:52.090
Stop him!

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:57.330
That was scary.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:02.380
He's holding himself back and making sure he doesn't start any trouble in his first game.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.830
Shigeno's pitching really well today.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.800
It's time we get some runs for him.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:20.910
Stop! Stop!

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:21.980
Hey!

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.640
Wh-What?!

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:24.920
He ignored the coach!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:32.910
Safe!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.510
Good job!

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:39.710
Nice run!

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:47.090
He did score, but ignoring the coach is pretty wild.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:50.550
If the catcher hadn't missed, he would've been out.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.200
You got real lucky.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.770
Well, we already had two outs,

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.650
and I don't dislike aggressive running.

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.070
Out!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.940
Well, now that we have a run,

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:11.450
I'll keep this inning down to zip.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:14.720
Hey, Japanese.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:19.830
You saw their pitcher hit me.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:23.130
You better not forget to get them back.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.300
And don't aim for some soft spot.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.380
Chest or higher.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.510
You can even hit him in the head.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.770
Don't worry.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:37.640
If a fight breaks out, I'll have your back.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:42.320
Is something wrong, Shigeno?

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.190
Oh, no.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.490
Nothing.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.080
Play!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.490
What did he say?

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:00.970
He wants me to hit a batter on purpose?

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:05.410
When my dad died from being hit by a pitch?

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.220
He must be joking!

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:12.510
That... is something I could never do!

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.650
Strike!

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.560
Time!

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:24.650
What?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.230
What's going on?

00:15:30.520 --> 00:15:31.680
What do you want?

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.070
I'm not tired enough to switch out yet.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:36.530
I see.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:42.880
I've heard that you Japanese are calm and dislike fights,

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.940
but that's just another way to say you're cowards.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.620
Say that again, bastard!

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:49.840
I—

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.940
I don't need an excuse for your cowardice.

00:15:52.940 --> 00:15:53.930
What's going on?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.410
In any case,

00:15:55.410 --> 00:16:02.100
you're not going to make your new teammate feel welcome, right?

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.470
Okay, okay.

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:06.610
I get it. Very well.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:19.360
What the hell did he say?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.200
Did he call me a coward?

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:27.750
Why do I have to hit their first batter and put him on base right after we scored?

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.380
Man...

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.800
Give me a break!

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:42.180
Bastard...

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:46.660
Ball!

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.810
Ball four!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.280
Damn!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:51.680
Time.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.340
What's wrong?

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.780
If something happened with Murdoch, then tell me.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:16:59.730
He's...

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:04.070
picking a fight with me for not hitting their batters.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:04.770
What?

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:11.740
Apparently, there's some unspoken rule about hitting the other team's batter if our batter gets hit,

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:15.260
but is that really something we have to do?

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:17.590
I don't know.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:22.940
First of all, it depends whether they hit our batter on purpose.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:27.930
If you don't like that stuff, you don't have to do it,

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:29.940
and he shouldn't be trying to force you to.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:34.340
I'll talk to Murdoch about it later,

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.240
so focus on the batter for now.

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:38.840
Play!

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.430
First base!

00:17:56.870 --> 00:17:57.820
Oops.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.690
It didn't come off my hand quite right.

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:09.660
Safe!

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.850
Where are you throwing?

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.030
You idiot!

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.470
You...

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.820
Give me a break!

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:28.330
You threw that ball wild on purpose because I didn't get them back!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.420
On purpose?!

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:35.600
My fingers were just a little sticky!

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:37.630
Stop! Both of you!

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.000
You better be kidding me!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.090
This is bad.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:44.050
Then before you try to make someone hit a batter,

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:47.560
do your own job and stop sucking!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.410
Wh-What did you say?

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.940
You bastard...

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.020
Go to hell!

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:57.030
H-Hey...

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.740
Are you okay, Roy?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.920
You...

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.510
I can't believe you did that!

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.820
Stop, Shigeno!

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.960
Bring it on!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.680
I'll beat you to a pulp!

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:08.830
That's enough, Murdoch!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.750
Shut up! Let me go!

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.160
Murdoch, you're out of here!

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.760
H-He's done it now.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.430
Get away from me.

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:31.110
You all right, Roy?

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.260
Yeah.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:34.080
He smashed my pretty face.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:34.970
Hey!

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:36.480
What's wrong, Keene?

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.880
It might be best if I sit out.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:46.240
It looks like...

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.160
I twisted my ankle when I fell.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.630
Wh-What?!

00:20:01.440 --> 00:20:03.580
Unbelievable!

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.910
That was an unbelievable way to lose.

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:08.670
You were the losing pitcher without giving up any runs,

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.040
and the team was stopped at four consecutive wins.

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:16.480
And with that stupid fight, Keene sprained his ankle, which will take two weeks to heal.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.940
I was so worried he'd jinx our streak,

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.330
and he did just that right off the bat.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.730
That stupid Murdoch...

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:29.330
Shigeno, what did you tell Murdoch after he made that error?

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:31.480
Oh.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:34.920
I complained because he made the error on purpose.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:35.910
On purpose?

00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:36.860
Yeah.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:41.090
Before that, he was trying to pick a fight with me.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.440
He told me to throw a payback pitch at them,

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:46.890
but I refused, and that error was how he got back at me.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.550
A payback pitch, huh?

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:52.660
Then he got mad at what I said, and that fight broke out.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.360
Man, that guy's crazy.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:58.160
But it's your fault too.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.570
H-How so?

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:04.470
Even if he picked a fight with you,

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:07.700
you can't know if the error was intentional.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:13.330
Besides, Murdoch wouldn't gain anything from making an error on purpose.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.480
Are you taking his side, Watts?

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:23.170
He's started tons of fights with his teammates in the past.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:27.660
In any case, he's just going to ruin the mood of our team.

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:32.290
If he continues to act like that, I'm sure the ones in charge will think twice about using him.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.250
So just have a little patience, Shigeno.

